  "name": "Pentose phosphate pathway",
  "category": "metabolic",
  "topic": "metabolism",
  "summary": "A cytosolic branch from glucose-6-phosphate. The oxidative phase produces NADPH (for reductive biosynthesis and antioxidant defence) and ribose-5-phosphate (for nucleotides); the non-oxidative phase interconverts sugars and returns carbon to glycolysis.",
  "evidence": "established",
  "layout": "chain",
  "location": "Cytosol",
  "net": "G6P + 2 NADP⁺ + H₂O → Ribulose-5-P + 2 NADPH + 2 H⁺ + CO₂ (oxidative phase)",
  "clinical": "G6PD deficiency: red cells cannot regenerate NADPH, glutathione stays oxidised, and oxidant drugs or fava beans trigger haemolysis (Heinz bodies).",
